{"seq":6,"slug":"churchill-legacy","title":"温斯顿·丘吉尔：历史影响与评价","stage":"DONE","category":"winston-churchill","categoryLabel":"温斯顿·丘吉尔","chapterCount":3,"docCount":8,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy","rating":{"composite":3.52,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.4,"coverage":2.5,"positioning":null,"strategic":5},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/leaders/12_winston-churchill/6_churchill-legacy","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"温斯顿-丘吉尔-历史影响与评价\">温斯顿·丘吉尔：历史影响与评价</h1><p>1965 年 1 月 30 日，伦敦圣保罗大教堂为一位平民举行了自 1914 年以来规模最大的国葬。泰晤士河畔码头的吊车纷纷低头致意，逾三十万人冒着严寒排队瞻仰灵柩。那一刻，温斯顿·丘吉尔（Winston Leonard Spencer-Churchill，1874—1965）已不再只是一位卸任首相，而被英国人当作国族意志的化身送别。本卷探讨的正是这场国葬之后六十年间，丘吉尔形象如何被塑造、被神化、又被反复审问的过程。</p>\n<p>与本系列其他各卷（生平、政治生涯、二战领导、演说与著述、冷战）不同，本卷不再复述&quot;他做了什么&quot;，而集中追问&quot;他留下了什么&quot;——历史地位如何确立，争议为何越演越烈，影响怎样延续至今。这三条线索彼此缠绕：正因为他被抬得极高，对他的批判才显得格外尖锐。</p>\n<p>第一章梳理盖棺定论的制度性标志：1965 年国葬、2002 年 BBC &quot;最伟大的英国人&quot;票选、1953 年诺贝尔文学奖，以及他作为&quot;文人政治家&quot;在英语世界记忆中的位置。这些荣誉共同构成了二十世纪后半叶英国主流叙事对丘吉尔的官方评价。</p>\n<p>第二章直面争议。帝国主义立场、对印度的种族化言论、1943 年孟加拉饥荒中的责任，以及围绕这些问题的当代史学论战，构成了对&quot;丘吉尔崇拜&quot;最有力的反诘。本卷力求呈现争论各方的证据与分歧，而非给出简单裁决。</p>\n<p>第三章考察持久影响：1946 年富尔顿&quot;铁幕演说&quot;如何为冷战提供话语框架、如何铸造英美&quot;特殊关系&quot;这一概念；&quot;最光辉的时刻&quot;又如何在脱欧、战时纪念等政治语境中被反复征用，成为可供调遣的象征资源。</p>\n<p>阅读本卷，读者应当带着这样一种自觉：对历史人物的评价从不是静止的结论，而是每一代人根据自身处境重新进行的协商。丘吉尔之所以至今仍是争论焦点，恰恰因为他触及了帝国、民族、战争与自由这些尚未在英国社会内部和解的命题。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"historical-standing","title":"历史地位与盖棺定论","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/historical-standing","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"state-funeral-and-national-mourning","title":"国葬与全民哀悼","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/historical-standing/state-funeral-and-national-mourning"},{"seq":2,"slug":"greatest-briton-and-public-memory","title":"最伟大的英国人与公众记忆","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/historical-standing/greatest-briton-and-public-memory"},{"seq":3,"slug":"nobel-prize-and-man-of-letters","title":"诺贝尔文学奖与文人政治家","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/historical-standing/nobel-prize-and-man-of-letters"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"controversies-and-reassessment","title":"争议与再评价","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/controversies-and-reassessment","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"empire-race-and-imperial-record","title":"帝国、种族与殖民记录","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/controversies-and-reassessment/empire-race-and-imperial-record"},{"seq":2,"slug":"bengal-famine-debate","title":"孟加拉饥荒的责任之争","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/controversies-and-reassessment/bengal-famine-debate"},{"seq":3,"slug":"modern-historiography-contest","title":"当代史学论战","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/controversies-and-reassessment/modern-historiography-contest"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"enduring-influence","title":"持久影响","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/enduring-influence","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"iron-curtain-and-special-relationship","title":"铁幕演说与英美特殊关系","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/enduring-influence/iron-curtain-and-special-relationship"},{"seq":2,"slug":"finest-hour-myth-and-political-invocation","title":"\"最光辉的时刻\"神话与政治征用","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/winston-churchill/churchill-legacy/enduring-influence/finest-hour-myth-and-political-invocation"}]}]}